h('CERTIFICATE OF APPROVAL'); para('This is to certify that the project entitled “AgriPredict: Crop Disease Detection and Farmer Advisory System” is a bonafide work of the students listed on the title page, submitted to the University of Mumbai in partial fulfilment of the requirements for the award of the Bachelor of Technology degree in Electronics and Telecommunication Engineering.'); para('\n\nGuide: ____________________     HOD: Dr. Girish Gidaye     Principal: Dr. Sangeeta Joshi'); br()
h('ACKNOWLEDGEMENT'); para('We express our sincere gratitude to our project guide, the faculty members of the Department of Electronics and Telecommunication Engineering, and Vidyalankar Institute of Technology for their guidance and support. We thank the department staff and our families for their encouragement. We also acknowledge the researchers and open-source communities whose datasets, libraries, and technical documentation informed AgriPredict.'); br()
h('DECLARATION'); para('We declare that this report presents our work in our own words and that ideas, results, and material from other sources are cited and listed in the references. We have not knowingly fabricated or falsified project data. Results attributed to this project are identified with their evaluation context and limitations.'); para('Date: ______________     Place: Mumbai'); table(['Sr. No.','Name','Roll No.','Signature'],[[i,'________________','____________','____________'] for i in range(1,5)]); br()
h('ABSTRACT'); para('AgriPredict is a web-based crop disease detection and farmer advisory project. It accepts a selected crop and leaf image, performs image-quality checks, and invokes a crop-specific classifier where a model is enabled. The system can return an uncertain result or request a retake when configured reliability conditions are not met. For accepted predictions, disease knowledge and language-model-assisted explanations provide context; a separate weather service presents current conditions and general advisory indicators. Weather is retrieved after image inference and is not an input to the disease classifier.'); para('The project team reports training models for apple, maize, grapes, tea, potato, cotton, sugarcane, groundnut, okra, and pumpkin. The first seven are reported hosted on Hugging Face; groundnut, okra, and pumpkin remain in notebooks. The current repository enables only apple and maize in live inference. Repository artifacts report apple internal test accuracy of 96.22%, macro-F1 of 0.9676, and OOD AUROC of 0.9631; these values do not establish field performance. Fertilizer recommendation and calculator modules are reported by the team, but their implementation and integration cannot be verified in the current source snapshot. The system uses React/Vite, FastAPI, PyTorch adapters, persistence services, and external weather and model-package services.'); para('Keywords: crop disease detection, image classification, selective prediction, farmer advisory, weather context, deep learning.'); br()
h('TABLE OF CONTENTS')
for x in ['Chapter 1 Introduction','1.1 Introduction | 1.2 Project Context and Motivation | 1.3 Aim and Contributions | 1.4 Report Organization','Chapter 2 Literature Review','2.1 Literature Survey | 2.2 Problem Statement | 2.3 Objectives | 2.4 Scope of Project','Chapter 3 Methodology','3.1 System Design | 3.2 Model Development and Crop Coverage | 3.3 Reliability-Aware Prediction | 3.4 Advisory and Data Handling','Chapter 4 Implementation','4.1 Architecture | 4.2 Backend Services | 4.3 Web Application | 4.4 Model Deployment | 4.5 Feature Status','Chapter 5 Experimental Results','5.1 Evidence Boundaries | 5.2 Apple Results | 5.3 Functional Behavior | 5.4 Limitations and Evaluation Plan','Chapter 6 Conclusion and Future Scope','References'] : para(x)
